$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A dry flask was charged with S5 (0.5 mmol), phenylboronic acid (91.4 mg,
0.75 mmol) and Na2CO3 (160 mg, 1.5 mmol), and toluene (3 mL) and H2O (2
mL) were added. The mixture was degassed under argon for 20 min, and
Pd(PPh3)4 (29 mg, 0.025 mmol) was added. The mixture was heated to 80 °C
overnight. H2O (30 mL) was added, and the mixture was extracted with Et2O
(40 mL × 2). The combined organic layers were dried over anhydrous MgSO4,
filtered and concentrated in vacuo. The residue was purified by flash
column chromatography to give 1p or 1z. 1p: Yield 75%; yellow oil.
analytical TLC (silica gel 60), 10% EtOAc in n-hexane, R f = 0.35; 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.89 (d, J = 6.7 Hz, 1H), 7.58-7.44 (m, 2H), 7.42-7.19
(m, 6H), 7.18-7.06 (m, 1H), 5.53 (s, 1H), 4.92 (s, 1H), 3.81 (s, 2H),
2.38-2.23 (m, 2H), 1.26-1.09 (m, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 172.0,
