$DATUM Ethyl
3-(3-(Naphthalen-1-yloxy)propyl)-7-(1,3,5-trimethyl-1H-pyrazol-4-yl)-1H-indole-2-carboxylate
(16). A suspension of boronate ester 15 (1.55 g, 3.10 mmol), cesium
carbonate (2.84 g, 8.73 mmol),
1,1′-bis(diphenylphosphino)ferrocenepalladium(II)
dichloride-dichloromethane complex (0.345 g, 0.422 mmol), and
4-iodo-1,3,5-trimethyl-1H-pyrazole (0.665 g, 2.82 mmol) in DMF (9.39 mL)
was heated to 100 °C for 30 min on a Biotage initiator microwave. The
reaction was diluted with EtOAc, filtered through a 2.5 g Celite SPE
column, and washed 2× with brine. The organic layer was dried over MgSO4,
filtered, and concentrated. The residue was purified by flash
chromatography (20-70% EtOAc/hexanes). 1.0 g (74%) of the title compound.
1H NMR (500 MHz, DMSO-d 6) δ 10.66 (s, 1H), 8.23-8.25 (m, 1H), 7.86-7.88
(m, 1H), 7.65 (d, J = 7.67 Hz, 1H), 7.49-7.55 (m, 2H), 7.45-7.47 (m, 1H),
7.37-7.41 (m, 1H), 7.01-7.09 (m, 2H), 6.91 (d, J = 7.67 Hz, 1H), 4.28 (q,
J = 7.06 Hz, 2H), 4.21-4.25 (m, 2H), 3.72 (s, 3H), 2.04 (s, 3H), 1.99 (s,
3H), 1.28 (t, J = 7.06 Hz, 3H). MS (LC/MS, APCI+) m/z 482.3 (M + H)+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki-Miyaura cross-coupling reaction
