$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of tetra-tert-butyl
4',4''',4''''',4'''''''-(pyrene-1,3,6,8-tetrayl)tetrakis
(2',5'-dimethyl-[1,1'-biphenyl]-4-carboxylate) (5): Compound 2 (1.8 g,
4.4 mmol, 4.4 equiv), 1,3,6,8-tetrabromopyrene (0.51 g, 1 mmol, 1 equiv),
PdCl2(dppf) (0.073 g, 0.1 mmol, 10 mol%) and K3PO4 (2.8 g, 13 mmol, 13
equiv) were added into a 150 mL Schlenk flask with a magnetic stir bar.
This mixture was evacuated for 15 minutes and the flask was refilled with
N2. Then degassed solvent 50 mL (dioxane:water=4:1) was added. The
reaction was heated at 90°C for 72 hours under an argon atmosphere. The
reaction was cooled down to RT and the crude mixture was diluted with 100
mL water and extracted three times with CHCl3 (3 x 200 mL). The organic
fractions were combined, dried with MgSO4 and evaporated to dryness, the
solid residue was dissolved in small amount of a 1:1 CH2Cl2–hexane
mixture and the compounds were separated by column chromatography
(hexanes to hexanes/CH2Cl2=1:4). Product 5 was isolated as a slightly
yellow solid (0.92 g, 0.7 mmol, 70%). 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.09 (d,
J = 8.3 Hz, 8H), 7.91 (d, J = 6.9 Hz, 2H), 7.88 (d, J = 4.7 Hz, 4H), 7.49
(d, J = 7.9 Hz, 8H), 7.34 (d, J = 6.1 Hz, 4H), 7.24 (d, J = 4.9 Hz, 4H),
2.34 – 2.27 (m, 12H), 2.20 – 2.08 (m, 12H), 1.64 (s, 36H). 13 C NMR (126
MHz, CDCl3) δ 165.92, 146.32, 140.48, 140.13, 134.54, 132.37, 131.33,
131.26, 130.63, 129.45, 129.32, 128.74, 125.63, 81.17, 77.41, 77.16,
76.91, 28.41, 20.09.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Schlenk tube used, Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Ultrahigh Surface Area Zirconium MOFs and Insights into the Applicability
of the BET Theory
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Wang, Timothy C.; Bury, Wojciech; Gomez-Gualdron, Diego A.; Vermeulen,
Nicolaas A.; Mondloch, Joseph E.; Deria, Pravas; Zhang, Kainan; Moghadam,
Peyman Z.; Sarjeant, Amy A.; Snurr, Randall Q.; Stoddart, J. Fraser;
Hupp, Joseph T.; Farha, Omar K.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2015), 137(10), 3585-3591

